Subject: [PATCH] Steps 9-10: fetch_documents, read_table_cells, workflows

Step 9 (complete Mike's read tools):
- fetch_documents: read several documents in one call with a shared size
  budget; tool guard skips docs already read and marks fetched ones as read
- read_table_cells: xlsx/csv as a table with column letters and real row
  numbers, sheet selection (Arabic names), Excel ranges (A1:F50, B:B, 3:20),
  header row always shown, paging, cell cap, values instead of formulas
- both count as evidence for the grounding check

Step 10 (workflows = saved prompt templates):
- workflows.py: SKILL.md folders parsed and validated with Agno's
  LocalSkills; shared + per-user (user overrides shared); read-only
  list_workflows / read_workflow tools (no script execution)
- AVAILABLE WORKFLOWS (names + descriptions) in the system prompt;
  /workflows and /wf <name> [text] to run one explicitly
- sample workflows: gazette-appointments, document-brief, compare-documents
- tests/test_step9_10.py

